# Client Security

## Never
- Read `*.properties`, `*.env*`, or secrets files.
- Log JWT, passwords, Xtream/M3U credentials, or refresh tokens (including Logcat).
- Return or display third-party source passwords in UI.
- Hardcode API keys, signing secrets, or encryption keys.

## Must
- Transport: HTTPS / TLS only toward backend.
- Persist session tokens via a **secure storage adapter** (Keystore / Keychain behind an interface).
- Treat source credentials as sensitive end-to-end; encrypt at rest when local cache is required.
- Validate/sanitize user-entered URLs and search strings at the boundary before use.
- QoE / crash telemetry: anonymous IDs only — no email or PII in payloads.

## Auth UX (MVP)
Email/password register, login, refresh, logout, reset-password against `/api/v1/auth/*`. One profile per account in MVP.
